  "result": "All 270 tests pass! \u2713\n\nI've successfully implemented foreign currency support to src/money.js:\n\n**RATES constant:**\n- `EUR: 1` (base currency)\n- `USD: 1.085` (units of USD per EUR)\n- `GBP: 0.8425` (units of GBP per EUR)\n\n**convert(cents, currency) function:**\n- Converts EUR cents to another currency\n- Returns `ok(amount in target currency's cents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Uses banker's rounding via roundCents for fractional conversions\n- Formula: `cents_in_target = eurcents \u00d7 rate`\n- Handles positive, negative, and zero amounts\n\n**formatMoney(cents, currency) function:**\n- Formats amounts in any currency with proper symbol and thousands separators\n- Currency symbols: `\u20ac` for EUR, `$` for USD, `\u00a3` for GBP\n- Format matches formatEuros: negative sign, symbol, thousands commas, 2 decimal places\n- Examples:\n  - `108500 USD \u2192 \"$1,085.00\"`\n  - `84250 GBP \u2192 \"\u00a3842.50\"`\n  - `-123456 EUR \u2192 \"-\u20ac1,234.56\"`\n\n**test/money.test.js - 16 new tests covering:**\n- RATES constant verification\n- Currency conversions (EUR\u2194USD, EUR\u2194GBP, EUR\u2194EUR)\n- Unknown currency error handling\n- Negative and zero amounts\n- Fractional conversions with banker's rounding\n- formatMoney with all currencies\n- Negative amounts with proper sign placement\n- Large amounts with thousands separators\n- Small amounts (cents precision)\n- Complete workflow: convert invoice amount to customer's currency and format\n\nThe implementation correctly handles exchange rate conversions, maintains cent precision, uses proper banker's rounding for fractional conversions, and formats all currencies consistently.",
